cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ResearchX — literature-grounded research assistant with verified citations"
message: "If ResearchX contributed to a paper, dataset, or review, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ResearchX contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xingguangYan/ResearchX"
url: "https://github.com/xingguangYan/ResearchX"
license: MIT
version: 4.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
keywords:
  - research-assistant
  - literature-review
  - systematic-review
  - prisma
  - citation-verification
  - agent-skills
  - claude-code
  - codex
abstract: >-
  ResearchX is an agent skill that runs the full research lifecycle: gap mining, method
  discovery, experiment design, manuscript writing, journal-fit upgrades, adversarial peer
  review, PRISMA systematic reviews, figures, and grant proposals. Every reference it emits
  is verified against Crossref, OpenAlex and arXiv, so fabricated citations are structurally
  prevented rather than merely discouraged.
